r I am  part of the DGA which is kind of cool as  well of all the festivals and events  that we had to get fortunate to be part  of the Student Academy Awards felt to me  like the most inclusive of the team  members and it really felt like we were  all included in winning it wasn't just  me and I think that's really important  because it really is a group effort to  make a film and I feel like we all  finished the week feeling like we were  all part of it we were all  it was so gratifying to see how well the  phone was received I think we played at  about 50 festivals over the course of  the year one about 25 Awards and my film  being a film in another language that  takes place in another country it was  really gratifying to see that that story  could be meaningful for people all over  the world my film won the college  Television Award Best Drama and Best  Director and the presenter of the Best  Director award was the producing  director of house Greg at anus and Greg  had seen the film obviously and really  admired it and wanted to know what I was  interested in doing so he invited me to  shadow the show and watch him work and  learn as much as I could from him and  four months later he offered me an  episode of the show to direct winning  the Student Academy Award really gave me  the credibility to allow Greg Katinas to  pitch me to the studios and networks  that produce house in order to get me  that job it was a really special show to  work on the opportunity to direct house  changed my life movies can change people  and I really really believe that and I'm  trying to tell the stories that I think  need to be told the most important thing  you can do as a young filmmaker  is just start creating material start  practicing it takes years and years to  find your voice I certainly don't feel  like I'm there yet I feel like I'm I'm  well on my way but I have a lot to learn  and I hope I never stop learning  you
 

